  "note": "Postponed election of the three councillors for Victoria Ward, Belfast Corporation, polled Thursday 19 June 1958: the poll of 21 May was cancelled on the death of the Unionist candidate Henry Fair (Belfast News-Letter, 27 May 1958, p. 6). Three of eight nominees withdrew (a Protestant Unionist and two Independent Unionists), leaving three Unionists and two Northern Ireland Labour (News-Letter, 5 June 1958, p. 5). Poll 36 per cent (News-Letter, p. 1). No change: the Unionists retained the three seats."
